Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:18:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix browser SIGSEGV when activating a vkd_* IME (Orca service
 removed)

Switching to (or typing in) a rule-based m17n layout could crash ash-chrome
outright with SIGSEGV at address 0x8 on the UI thread:

  EditorServiceConnector::BindEditor
  -> mojo::Remote<orca::mojom::...>::operator->  (null: remote was reset)
  <- EditorMediator::ResetEditorConnections
  <- EditorMediator::OnActivateIme
  <- NativeInputMethodEngineObserver::OnActivate

colorburst removed Gemini but not the Orca ("help me write") editor. Its
backing service is never registered, so content::ServiceProcessHost::Launch
drops the pipe and reset_on_disconnect() unbinds remote_orca_service_connector_.
The next IME activation reaches ResetEditorConnections (kOrcaServiceConnection is
still enabled by default) and calls straight through the now-null remote.

This became reachable for every vkd_* layout once the routing fix sent the whole
m17n extension through NativeInputMethodEngine (which owns the editor sink); the
plain InputMethodEngine never invoked the editor path. It is a latent crash for
the shipping Telex path too, under enough IME switching.

Guard EditorServiceConnector::BindEditor to no-op when the Orca remote is not
bound. When Orca is actually present (branded builds) this changes nothing.

VERIFIED on device (colorburst R153, instance 2, owner imetail): before, a couple
of IME switches + typing crashed the browser to a session-restore "Recap" dialog
(minidump: SIGSEGV 0x8, stack above). After, switching among
telex/vni/viqr/tcvn/Thai/Arabic and typing in each no longer crashes.



---
 .../ash/input_method/editor_service_connector.cc      | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/editor_service_connector.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/editor_service_connector.cc
index 1fa72a89a0..51c4a27d02 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/editor_service_connector.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/editor_service_connector.cc
@@ -38,6 +38,17 @@ void EditorServiceConnector::BindEditor(
     mojo::PendingAssociatedRemote<orca::mojom::SystemActuator> system_actuator,
     mojo::PendingAssociatedRemote<orca::mojom::TextQueryProvider>
         text_query_provider) {
+  // colorburst: the Orca/editor ("help me write") backing service is not
+  // shipped (Gemini removed). content::ServiceProcessHost::Launch then drops
+  // the connection and reset_on_disconnect() unbinds this remote, so calling
+  // through it dereferences a null proxy and SIGSEGVs the browser on the next
+  // IME activation (ResetEditorConnections) -- reached for every vkd_* layout
+  // now that they route through NativeInputMethodEngine's editor sink. Never
+  // call into an unbound service; a no-op guard when Orca is actually present.
+  // See internal-knowledge/VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md.
+  if (!IsBound()) {
+    return;
+  }
   remote_orca_service_connector_->BindEditor(
       std::move(system_actuator), std::move(text_query_provider),
       std::move(editor_client_connector), std::move(editor_event_sink),
